items.a:
A build runs the CPU flat out for many minutes - the shader stage is the heaviest. When the app disappears mid-build, the system killed it, for one of three reasons:

· The battery manager clears "abnormal power drain" - a heavy app is force-stopped, on MIUI even in the foreground;
· Not enough free memory - a build peaks at several GB, and games or video apps left in the background push it out;
· Low battery - below a threshold the system throttles the CPU and clears backgrounds on its own, so builds die earlier and run slower.

To make a build succeed (in order):
1. Clear the memory: swipe away games, video players and other heavy apps before you start;
2. Keep the battery healthy: build plugged in, power-saver modes off, and do not start below 20%;
3. Set nx2androidX's battery policy to "No restrictions" (MIUI: Battery → App smart battery; Huawei/Honor: App launch management → Manual; Samsung: out of the "Sleeping apps" list);
4. In the phone manager / Security app: allow background runs and autostart;
5. Lock the app's card in the recents screen;
6. Keep the screen on and the app in front while it builds.

If it dies anyway, just start again: every finished stage is cached, it catches up in seconds.

Check the following in order:

1. Switch to a different Vulkan driver in Settings and try again;
2. Review the log of that build (build details → "Share log") to confirm the port is complete;
3. If the crashes began after importing save data, and every launch fails (typically around the title screen), the save data is most likely incompatible with this environment. Open the game's detail panel and run "Manage → Delete the saves", then start the game again. To keep that save for investigation, export it first.

Save data is installed as-is; the app performs no content conversion. Saves exported by other emulators (Eden, yuzu, Ryujinx, etc.) or console tools may carry internal state this environment cannot read, and in some cases the game will crash on launch. It is recommended to:

1. Export the current save data as a backup before importing;
2. Confirm the save comes from the same game version as this port (including updates and DLC state);
3. If the game crashes on every launch after importing, run "Manage → Delete the saves" and start over.
